From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: meta-rzg3l-fast-boot-base <fastboot@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] configs: smarc-rzg3l: fast-boot default environment

Bake the fast-boot U-Boot environment into the built-in defaults so the
board does not need a manual setenv/saveenv session after flashing.

Three changes, all inside the non-distro-boot branch of the header, which
is the branch smarc-rzg3l_defconfig selects (CONFIG_RZG3L_DISTRO_BOOT is
not set there):

1. bootcmd loses the leading "env default -a".

   The stock value is "env default -a;run bootcmd_check;run bootimage".
   That reset runs on every boot and reverts the whole environment to the
   built-in defaults, so any saved fast-boot tuning is thrown away one
   command before it would have been used. It also makes the environment
   effectively read-only, which is not what a product wants.

2. prodemmcbootargs / prodsdbootargs lose "earlycon" and gain
   "quiet systemd.show_status=false".

   earlycon replays the kernel ring buffer synchronously over the
   115200-baud UART, and every subsequent printk is emitted at the same
   speed. quiet raises the console loglevel so only warnings and above
   reach the UART, and systemd.show_status=false stops systemd printing a
   status line per unit. The records are still in the kernel log and the
   journal; only the serial output is suppressed.

   Re-add earlycon when debugging an early kernel failure - it is the only
   way to see output from before the real console is registered.

   Both variables are changed, not just the eMMC one, so an SD boot of the
   same image behaves identically. bootcmd_check picks between them.

3. bootdelay is not touched here. It comes from CONFIG_BOOTDELAY through
   env_default.h, so it is set to 0 in fastboot.cfg instead.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [configuration]
---
 include/configs/smarc-rzg3l.h | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/configs/smarc-rzg3l.h b/include/configs/smarc-rzg3l.h
index 96384fd..de14dd7 100644
--- a/include/configs/smarc-rzg3l.h
+++ b/include/configs/smarc-rzg3l.h
@@ -122,14 +122,14 @@
 #define CFG_EXTRA_ENV_SETTINGS \
 	"usb_pgood_delay=2000\0" \
 	"bootm_size=0x10000000\0" \
-	"prodsdbootargs=setenv bootargs rw rootwait earlycon root=/dev/mmcblk1p2 \0" \
-	"prodemmcbootargs=setenv bootargs rw rootwait earlycon root=/dev/mmcblk0p2 \0" \
+	"prodsdbootargs=setenv bootargs rw rootwait root=/dev/mmcblk1p2 quiet systemd.show_status=false\0" \
+	"prodemmcbootargs=setenv bootargs rw rootwait root=/dev/mmcblk0p2 quiet systemd.show_status=false\0" \
 	"bootimage=booti 0x48080000 - 0x48000000 \0" \
 	"emmcload=ext4load mmc 0:2 0x48080000 boot/Image;ext4load mmc 0:2 0x48000000 boot/r9a08g046l48-smarc.dtb;run prodemmcbootargs \0" \
 	"sd1load=ext4load mmc 1:2 0x48080000 boot/Image;ext4load mmc 1:2 0x48000000 boot/r9a08g046l48-smarc.dtb;run prodsdbootargs \0" \
 	"bootcmd_check=if mmc dev 1; then run sd1load; else run emmcload; fi \0"
 
-#define CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND "env default -a;run bootcmd_check;run bootimage"
+#define CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND "run bootcmd_check;run bootimage"
 #endif
 
 /* For board */
